  "unresolved_questions": [
    "PWR-003 (600 mA on +3V3) conflicts with PWR-004 (500 mA maximum draw from the USB host): a 600 mA continuous 3.3 V rail from a 5 V LDO exceeds the 500 mA VBUS budget. Proposal: keep the LDO rated at 600 mA for transmit peaks, add sufficient bulk capacitance (>= 10 uF plus 100 uF optional) to absorb Wi-Fi bursts, and revise PWR-003 to 'peak' rather than 'continuous', or authorize a >500 mA source (USB-C 1.5 A advertisement or higher-current host).",
    "Connector change: replacing J1 (Connector:USB_B_Micro) with a USB-C 2.0 16-pin receptacle plus CC1/CC2 5.1 kOhm pulldowns changes the footprint and pin count. Confirm USB-C is required (per IF-005) versus amending the request to micro-B.",
    "ESP32-WROOM-32 has no native USB PHY, yet USB_D+/USB_D- currently connect J1 directly to U1.6/U1.7. Confirm insertion of BLK-USB-UART (e.g. CP2102N or CH340N) and removal of the direct J1-to-module USB nets; alternatively switch to an ESP32-S3 module with native USB.",
    "Regulator topology: a linear LDO at 5 V -> 3.3 V and 500 mA dissipates ~0.85 W, which stresses TEMP-003 (< 40 C rise) and worsens TEMP-002 self-heating error. Confirm whether a buck converter is acceptable, or whether the LDO must be used for cost/EMI simplicity with an enlarged copper thermal pad.",
    "Sensor thermal placement: MECH-006 requires >= 15 mm separation, but board self-heating still couples through the ground pour. Confirm whether a thermal-relief slot or pour split around U2 is permitted on a 2-layer stackup.",
    "GPIO25 disposition: expose as a test point/header (allows future use) or mark as explicit no-connect for TEST-003. Recommend a test point.",
    "Whether a boot-mode push-button and reset push-button are wanted, or whether DTR/RTS auto-reset from the bridge alone is sufficient.",
    "No cost ceiling, build quantity, or certification target (FCC/CE) was supplied; these bound COST-001 and antenna/keep-out treatment and remain open pending stakeholder input.",
    "USB VBUS-to-3V3 reverse-current and ESD protection level: confirm whether a dedicated ESD array on D+/D-/VBUS and a series input ferrite/fuse are in scope for BLK-VBUS-PROT."
  ]
}
